
Documentation:
    ☐ Create a `wiki/usage.md` document for describing how to setup a project to use the test runner.
    ☐ Create a `wiki/mounting.md` document from the latest `non-owning-native-screen-mount-proposal.md` document.
    ☐ Create a `wiki/commands.md` document to describe the available commands for the test runner.
    ☐ Create a `wiki/writing-tests.md` document to describe how to write DwarfSpec tests.

Frontend:
    ☐ Create a test-runner UI for running and debugging tests, including a test results panel and test command logs.
    ☐ test-runner UI should have the ability to re-run failed tests.
    ☐ test-runner UI should have the ability to filter tests by tags or categories.
    ☐ test-runner UI should have the ability to click through command log items and see the snapshots of the component tree at that point in time.

Testing Features:
    ☐ DwarfSpec should detect what the initial screen focus is and at the end of a test it should automatically detect if the test is leaving the screen focus on a different base-game widnow than it started, and if so, it should log a warning.
        Things which are explicitly MOUNTED by a test dont count, this detection and warning must occur after the normal test teardown and unmounting of any mounted components.
    ☐ Explore possible ways to prevent user keyboard/mouse input from interfering with the test runner, such as a "lock" mode that prevents user input while tests are running.
    ☐ Refactor `ds.get()` so it is more like a Cypress get assertion, returning a `DSQuery` object that can be chained with `.should(...)` and `.find(...)` methods.
        - get method will become more of an async query with a timeout.
        - get method acts as an implicit assertion.
        - allows for more complex queries and assertions on the component tree.
    ☐ Update `ds.get(...)` to accept and parse simple CSS-like selector queries.
    ☐ Evaluate possible useful commands that can be added for non-ui (behavioral) game logic testing, such as `ds.get_state(...)`, `ds.set_state(...)`, `ds.spy(...)` (for DF game events), `ds.trigger_event(...)`, etc.
